Understanding the Workflow

    User Submission:
        User logs in with credentials (admin-assigned).
        Fills out a form:
            Chooses removal terms (returnable/non-returnable).
            If returnable: Shows dateTo and department.
            If non-returnable: Shows dateFrom and employee (sender).
            Fills itemDescription (free text).
            Selects removalReason from a dropdown; if “Other,” a text field appears for custom reason.
            Uploads multiple images of the item.
        Reviews all fields, edits if needed, then submits.
    Approval Process:
        Form goes to the user’s department manager (HOD).
        HOD reviews, approves, or rejects with a reason.
        If approved, it moves to Finance, then MOD, then Security.
        Each level can approve (with signature) or reject (with reason).
        If rejected at any stage, the user gets a notification with the reason.
    Final Steps:
        If Security approves, a report is generated, and the user gets a printable form (the one you provided).
        If rejected, the user is notified with the rejection reason.

Database Model Adjustments

We need to update the Prisma schema to handle:

    User Auth: A User model for credentials and roles.
    Removal Reasons: A separate RemovalReason model for the dropdown options.
    Images: A one-to-many relation for item images.
    Approval Status: Track the form’s status and rejection reason.
    Signatures: Already included as base64 strings.


